 Vroom Enhanced 2.0b (23.11.2026)
 Original install: Mr.Larmer, CFou. Version 2.0b: Vesuri.

 This install applies to "Vroom (& Data Disk)" © 1991-92 Lankhor.

 This install requires WHDLoad 16 or newer, DIC, RawDIC and The Patcher to be in the path.
 The programs can be found in the WHDLoad package.
 To install from a different drive than DF0: select installation mode Expert.

 The installed program requires 0.5 MB ChipMem and 0.5 MB OtherMem.
 It can be quit by pressing F10 (key can be changed with Tooltype "QuitKey=").

 If you have problems with this installation please try and get a newer
 version of this package from the WHDLoad WWW-Page. If that doesn't help try
 some Tooltypes like NOCACHE, NOAUTOVEC, EXPCHIP, NOMMU, PAL or NTSC. If
 that also fails, please inform the author via the Bug-Report-Form which
 can be accessed on the WHDLoad WWW-Page.

 For the full WHDLoad package, other installs and updates refer to:
	http://www.whdload.de/
 or	aminet:dev/misc/whdload#?
 and	aminet:game/patch/

 version 2.0b (23.11.2026) done by Vesuri
 - fixed the black screen and crash with CPU caches on (68020-68060)
 - fixed a crash on fast CPUs (68060) in races
 - fixed flickering roadside objects and too fast menu wipes on fast CPUs
 - fixed the keyboard handshake, which was too short on every CPU
 - fixed the data disk's crash at its first race
 - the drive motor is left to WHDLoad

 version 1.4 (03.06.06) done by CFou
 - ExitKey fixed for 68000
 - Colored icons included
 - Source code included
 - New install script

 version 1.0 & 1.3 done by Mr.Larmer
 - initial release
 - data disk must be installed in the same dir like Vroom,
 - a lot of blitter waits added,
 - disk protection removed,
 - self modyfing code removed,
 - save highscore to HD,
 - nice NI/MWB icons included,

 Thanx to Harry (Vroom) and Adrian Simpson (data disk) for original disk image.

Mr.Larmer/Wanted Team in 2000.
